{
"answer": "In lipid metabolism disorders like Gaucher disease, a lack of or malfunctioning enzymes prevents the body from converting fats (lipids) into energy [MLP-6387]. This causes a harmful buildup of lipids in the body, which over time damages cells and tissues, particularly in the brain, peripheral nervous system, liver, spleen, and bone marrow [MLP-6387]. Specifically in Gaucher disease, insufficient glucocerebrosidase leads to fatty substance accumulation in the spleen, liver, lungs, bones, and sometimes the brain, impairing organ function [MLP-1523]."
}
